          "id": "monthly-cost",
          "title": "Estimated monthly cost by volume",
          "description": "Select A, B or C to see its monthly estimates at each volume. Total = database + data + processing. A/B use a dedicated 2 vCPU / 8 GB database (~US$ 134, double with HA). C uses a small instance (~US$ 15). Data: ~200 B per Postgres row, ~20 B per Parquet row, ~30 items per subscription. A/B use Datastream CDC at US$ 2 per GiB in the model. Processing: ~US$ 5 per 100 million at 500 records/s on 1 vCPU. Excludes data lake and engineering time. The model uses approximate São Paulo Cloud SQL pricing and R$ 5.55 per US dollar (reference closing rate R$ 5.56). Up to 100 million records, the database instance dominates the estimate. Study scale: 158 million active subscriptions. A and C write about 4.7 billion records at roughly 30 items per subscription. A needs a larger instance. B writes 158 million rows. C at the same subscription grain is about US$ 25.",
